text:
The keyframe comparison showed three problems, and this revision fixes all three:

- **Turned frames (3930 to 5470 ms) were badly off.**
  - **Too big and too wide.** The body was stretched too deep and the camera was too close, so it filled the whole frame. It is now close to its normal depth and the camera is at about the frame-1 distance. The profile should come out about 120 px wide, like the GIF.
  - **Head pushed backwards.** It is now centred, and the turn angle is about -1.2 rad so some of the belly shows, as in the GIF.
  - **Eye and hand placement.** The visible eye now sits on the side of the head, which puts it near where the GIF shows it. The near hand hangs behind the back in the last keyframe.
- **Head looked like a separate ball.** The top of the body now rises into the head with a smooth pear shape instead of a notch at the shoulders. The top of the body is slightly flattened front-to-back so it doesn't cover the face, mouth or cheeks.
- **Frames 800 to 3130 ms.** The head is narrower and sits more naturally on the body. The prop and hands are adjusted to the new mouth height, and the camera is shifted so the character sits further left, as in the GIF.

I couldn't render it here; these numbers are worked out from the code and the keyframes, not measured from new frames.

